[BEGIN]
  ObjTp=Hd
  Cmn1=UDP Broadcast and Receive v2.0\\\\4-Series. This socket defaults||1
  Cmn2=to UDP 50001.\\\\A CR or LF ends one received datagram. Two processor||1
  Cmn3=announces have\\neither, so two of those can still arrive as one||1
  Cmn4=buffer.\\\\Received strings and Enable_FB are written only when||1
  Cmn5=the value changes.\\Packet_Rx still pulses for every accepted packet.
  Cmn6=\\\\Reply uses the one SIMPL+ UDP socket. It is aimed at the sender,||1
  Cmn7=then\\put back on 255.255.255.255. A datagram in that gap can be||1
  Cmn8=missed.\\\\A stored MAC whose length is not 12 or 17 is published||1
  Cmn9=as\\00:00:00:00:00:00. Own packets are dropped and are not answered.
  Cmn10=\\\\Press F1 for UDP Beacon and Extract v2.0.html. That file is||1
  Cmn11=also the\\help for UDP Extract Data v2.0. Leave it next to both||1
  Cmn12=modules.\\\\-- VERSION HISTORY --\\v2.0  2026-10-19\\- 2026-11-03:
  Cmn13=||1F1 opens UDP Beacon and Extract v2.0.html, shared with Extract\\
  Cmn14=- 2026-11-02: CR or LF ends one received datagram, so a second copy\\
  Cmn15=||2concatenated in SocketRxBuf is not stored in Received_Data\\-||1
  Cmn16=2026-11-02: Received_* and Enable_FB update only when the value||1
  Cmn17=changes\\- Announce_Interval heartbeat (0s off, default 5s). Use||1
  Cmn18=15s or 30s when\\  hundreds of processors share the port\\- Reply||1
  Cmn19=off by default. On answers each new sender once, then waits through\\
  Cmn20=||260s of silence, and sends at most one reply every 0.5 s\\- Packet_Rx||1
  Cmn21=pulses after the four received strings are written\\- Re-open the||1
  Cmn22=socket if Enable is high and the listen socket drops\\\\v1.3  2026-
  Cmn23=09-09\\- Prior symbol, left in the tree unchanged\\
[END]
